# Accepted residual CVEs for the render image (ttlequals0/audicle-render).
# Concatenated with .trivyignore by scripts/trivy_gate.sh for the render scan.
# Do not pass this file to the app or tts scans.
# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck all retained entries: 2026-10-10.

# -- render image only (python:3.12-slim + xvfb + mesa for Camoufox browser):

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
# xserver-common / xvfb: Xvfb runs as uid 1000 with one screen and
# TCP disabled. CVE-2023-5574 requires legacy multi-screen Zaphod mode and a
# cross-screen pointer warp during reset. The configured single screen does
# not use that mode.
# Remove when Debian ships fixes or the render image drops Xvfb.
CVE-2023-5574

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
# libcups2t64 (HIGH x1): CVE-2026-34980 is in the cupsd scheduler's handling of
# an unauthenticated Print-Job to a shared PostScript queue, followed by PPD
# control-record reparsing. The image contains only libcups for GTK; it contains
# no cupsd or cups-browsed daemon and configures no print queue, so the affected
# server code and network endpoint are absent. Remove when Debian ships a patch.
CVE-2026-34980

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
# libxml2 (CRITICAL x1, "affected"): CVE-2026-6653 is a use-after-free in
# xmlParseInternalSubset on crafted XML. The system library is linked by LLVM
# and update-mime-database, but not by the Camoufox executable, libxul,
# libmozgtk, or its bundled dependent-library list. Gecko parses hostile page
# XML/SVG with its own parser; page bytes do not reach system libxml2. Added
# 0.48.2. Remove when Debian trixie ships a patched libxml2.
CVE-2026-6653

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
# libtiff6 (HIGH x1, "will_not_fix"): CVE-2026-36849 is a DoS via a large
# SamplesPerPixel tag. libtiff is linked only by GTK's dynamically loaded GDK
# Pixbuf TIFF loader; Camoufox/Gecko does not link it and does not route hostile
# page images through GDK Pixbuf. The sidecar has no path that asks GTK to open a
# local TIFF, so the vulnerable decoder is installed but unreachable. Debian
# marks it will_not_fix for trixie. Added 0.48.3. Remove if a patch ships.
CVE-2026-36849

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
# libtiff6 (HIGH x1, "affected"), added 0.56.9: CVE-2026-52490 is arbitrary
# code execution in process_command_opts() in tools/tiffcrop.c. That code is
# the tiffcrop CLI, which ships in libtiff-tools; the render image installs
# only libtiff6, so the vulnerable function is not present in the image at all.
# No fix released. Remove when Debian ships a patched libtiff.
CVE-2026-52490

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
# Debian 13 has no fixed package versions. The system libxml2 is present through
# shared-mime-info and Mesa; its vulnerable Python bindings are not installed.
# Python lxml bundles libxml2 2.14.6. Camoufox's executable and dependent-library
# list do not link system libxml2 or Expat. System Expat is used by fontconfig,
# Mesa, and D-Bus for local configuration, not fetched page data.
CVE-2026-74860
CVE-2026-86140
CVE-2026-76956
CVE-2026-76957
# Added 0.58.0 under the same reasoning, no fixed Debian package yet:
# libexpat1 CVE-2026-66046 and CVE-2026-93990, and libxml2 CVE-2026-86138,
# CVE-2026-86139, CVE-2026-86142, CVE-2026-86143, CVE-2026-86144.
CVE-2026-66046
CVE-2026-93990
CVE-2026-86138
CVE-2026-86139
CVE-2026-86142
CVE-2026-86143
CVE-2026-86144

# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10. Added 0.58.5.
# libx11 (CVE-2026-88806) and libxrender1 (CVE-2026-88807), HIGH, "affected":
# heap overflows in the X client when it parses replies from a malicious X server.
# The only X server here is the container's own Xvfb, started by the entrypoint
# under the browser's unprivileged uid with TCP disabled. Pages cannot act as an X
# server. No fixed trixie package yet. Remove when Debian ships patches.
CVE-2026-88806
CVE-2026-88807

# libxtst6 parses replies from a malicious X server. DISPLAY is pinned to the
# local Xvfb above; page content cannot supply an X server. No trixie fix.
# https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-94286
# Owner: Audicle maintainers. Recheck: 2026-10-10.
CVE-2026-94286
